# Cursor Rules for WelineFramework

⚠️ **CRITICAL:** Host bootstrap only — framework hard rules live in MCP `hard-constraints.v1`.

## Quick Start
1. Run `php app/code/Weline/Ai/Mcp/scripts/ensure-project-guidance.php` → `status=ready`
2. Call MCP `prepare_project` on `dev`; read `agent_guidance.hard_constraints`
3. Call `resolve_task_context` for task-scoped `workflow_contract.v1`
4. Authority: `app/code/Weline/Ai/doc/AI硬规则索引.md` + owning module `doc/`

## Core Protocols
- Follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for MCP attach / readiness / native-fallback gates
- Never ask the user to hand-edit Cursor MCP Settings; never call `mcp_auth` for this STDIO MCP

## Commands
```bash
php bin/w setup:upgrade              # 全量升级（Schema、路由、注册表等）
php bin/w setup:upgrade --route      # 选填：仅刷新路由（新增/变更控制器后，跳过 Schema）
php bin/w http:request / [-b|-api]   # Route test
php bin/w server:reload|restart -r   # WLS lifecycle
```

Framework constraints (no `generated/`, no `routes.xml`, Theme/Taglib/i18n, etc.) are enforced via MCP hard constraints — do not duplicate them here.
